  "pricing_chart": {
    "families": ["haiku", "sonnet", "opus", "fable"],
    "rule": "Derived, not typed: each family's bars are its newest generally available release's price_in / price_out; the dashed `prev` mark is the price the family carried before its most recent change, named after the last release that had it and dated to the first release at the current price. Mythos is priced like Fable but restricted, so it gets no bars.",
    "source": "Claude API pricing docs",
    "source_url": "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing",
    "as_of": "2026-11-09",
    "history": [
      "Claude API list pricing (per million tokens) as of November 9, 2026, from platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing. Fable 5.2 (Nov 9, 2026) is the first Fable price cut: $8/$40, down from the $10/$50 Fable 5 and Fable 5.1 held (cache reads $0.20, still 2.5% of input; cache writes $10 5m / $16 1h; Batch $4/$20; fast mode $16/$80; 1M context at the standard rate). Claude Mythos 5.2 is priced identically to Fable 5.2 but restricted to verified organizations, so it isn't given its own bars. Sonnet 5's $2/$10, announced as introductory pricing through Aug 31, 2026, was made permanent in September (the scheduled rise to $3/$15 was cancelled), so the intro overlay is gone. Opus 5.5 (Sep 22, 2026) is the first Opus price cut since Opus 4.5: $4/$20, down from the $5/$25 the tier held from Opus 4.5 through Opus 5. Sonnet 5.5 (Sep 28, 2026) replaces Sonnet 5 as the current Sonnet at the same $2/$10 (cache reads $0.20 at launch, halved to $0.10 on Oct 7, 2026 per the Haiku 5.5 announcement); Sonnet 5 stays on the API. Haiku 5.5 (Oct 7, 2026) is priced by prompt length, the only current Claude model that is: $0.10/$0.50 for prompts up to 100k tokens and $0.50/$2.50 above (cache reads $0.01 / $0.05, 5m cache writes $0.125 / $0.625, Batch half), per the pricing docs' model and long-context tables. The bars show the up-to-100k rate; `long` carries the over-100k rate into the tooltips. Haiku 4.5 stays on the API at $1/$5. prev is the tier's list price before its most recent change, drawn dashed: Haiku 4.5's $1/$5 fell 90% with Haiku 5.5 (Oct 7, 2026); Sonnet 4.6's $3/$15 fell a third with Sonnet 5 (Jun 30, 2026); Opus 5's $5/$25 fell 20% with Opus 5.5 (Sep 22, 2026); Fable 5.1's $10/$50 fell 20% with Fable 5.2 (Nov 9, 2026)."
    ]
  },
